-### Subtopics
--   **Multi-Level Array Grid:** Uses array-based indexing for variable depth subdivision. Choose when scene density varies significantly across different regions and a fixed $M$ is insufficient.
--   **Multi-Grid Ray Traversal:** May involve multiple distinct grids or more complex hierarchical structures. Choose when the scene has distinct geometric components that benefit from separate acceleration structures.
--   **Two-Level Grids for Ray Tracing on GPUs:** Optimized specifically for GPU architectures with specific memory coalescing requirements. Choose when targeting GPU hardware with limited shared memory.
--   **Multi-resolution grids:** General term for grids with varying resolution. Choose when the scene has high-frequency details in some areas and low-frequency in others, requiring adaptive refinement rather than fixed blocks.
+## Subtopics
+
+### Multi-Grid
+An approach based on adopting a coarse grid at the first stage of reconstruction to obtain a rapid, reliable initial volume estimate [S5, unofficial]. It reduces the problem dimension by compressing images while maintaining a 1:1 resolution ratio between voxels and pixels, using a subsampling factor (e.g., $f_c = 2$) to limit noise amplification [S5, unofficial].
+
+### Speculative Macrocell Grid Traversal
+An extension of macrocell grid traversal that advances each ray through up to $N_{Spec}$ visible blocks instead of just one, recording multiple block IDs to increase GPU utilization and terminate rays in fewer passes [S6]. The kernel is run over all $w \times h$ pixels; terminated rays exit early [S6]. Calculate offset $o = O_{Act}[ray] \times N_{Spec}$ [S6]. Write up to $N_{Spec}$ visible block IDs into $R_{BID}$ starting at $o$ [S6]. If the ray exits the volume early, fill remaining $R_{BID}$ entries with $UINT\_MAX$ [S6]. Write $N_{Spec}$ entries of the ray ID into $R_{ID}$ starting at $o$ [S6]. Save coarse and fine grid iterator states after $N_{Spec}$ visible blocks are found to resume traversal later [S6].
 
 ## Operating characteristics
--   **Time Complexity:** Build time is $O(N^3)$ for the fine grid, but the macrocell build is $O((N/M)^3)$ which is trivial. Traversal time is reduced by skipping empty macrocells. The overhead of checking macrocells is minimal.
--   **Memory Complexity:** Adds $O((N/M)^3)$ bits (or bytes) for the macrocell grid. For $M=6$, this is roughly $1/216$ of the fine grid size, which is negligible.
+-   **Time Complexity:** Build time is $O(N^3)$ for the fine grid, but the macrocell build is $O((N/M)^3)$ which is trivial [S2, S3]. Traversal time is reduced by skipping empty macrocells. The overhead of checking macrocells is minimal [S2, S3].
+-   **Memory Complexity:** Adds $O((N/M)^3)$ bits (or bytes) for the macrocell grid. For $M=6$, this is roughly $1/216$ of the fine grid size, which is negligible [G].
 -   **Measured Performance:** Approximately 30% improvement over single ray grids for medium-sized animated scenes [S2, S3].
